is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: dns_server
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: DNS service (BIND/named) on dns_server. The DNS daemon is up and listening on 10.200.0.2:53, but its configuration is incorrect for client resolution.

Mechanism: host_1_1_1_1 can reach servers by IP (curl http://10.200.0.3 is fast; ICMP OK), but any name-based access hangs/fails because DNS lookups are refused. From host_1_1_1_1, nslookup web_server_0 10.200.0.2 returns “REFUSED,” and ping web_server_0 fails with “Temporary failure in name resolution.” This causes applications to delay/retry DNS until they time out.

Localization: dns_server’s BIND instance. Evidence on the device:
- named is running (/usr/sbin/named -f -u bind) and listening on 10.200.0.2:53 (ss -plntu).
- /etc/bind/named.co
